# Parser Bot Rules (MANDATORY)

## Event DTO
- Every item MUST have:
  - source
  - raw_id (stable per source)
  - checksum (content-based, deterministic)
  - published_at (ISO 8601)
- DO NOT generate random IDs for dedup.

## Dedup
- Dedup MUST be applied before publishing.
- Use raw_id and/or checksum as the source of truth (as defined by the project).
- Retries MUST NOT republish duplicates.

## Delivery Idempotency
- Publishing must be safe to retry:
  - detect previously delivered items
  - skip duplicates deterministically
- If delivery fails mid-way, the next run must resume safely without duplicates.

## Time Rules
- published_at MUST be ISO 8601.
- Normalize timezone consistently.

## Patch Discipline
- Keep pipeline changes minimal:
  - collector OR processor OR publisher changes should be localized unless explicitly requested.
